# Research docs (not part of the tool)
PREMISE.md
PMF-ASSESSMENT.md
# COMPETITORS.md was ignored here until 2026-07-29. It is now tracked and public
# at docs/COMPETITORS.md, purged of uniqueness claims. An untracked input to
# launch copy is an unverified claim with a clear path to a public surface.
DISTRIBUTION.md
ECONOMICS.md

# Audit scaffolding (internal analysis, not part of the tool).
# `analysis/*` rather than `analysis/`: git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is excluded, and the two entries below must be re-includable.
analysis/*
# The labelled corpora and the measurement harness are the evidence behind the
# efficacy figures published in the README and SHIP-READINESS.md. A reader who
# cannot inspect the corpus cannot check the claim, so these are tracked. Until
# 2026-07-29 only holdout_v2 and html_v1 were committed (via force-add) and the
# 67 items behind the headline figures were not, which made those figures
# unreproducible from a clean clone.
!analysis/corpus/
!analysis/measure_efficacy.py
# The real-page base-rate measurement, added 2026-07-29. `measure_base_rate.py`
# produces published figures, so it is tracked for the same reason as the harness
# above. `build_realpage_corpus.py` is tracked because a corpus nobody can rebuild
# is evidence nobody can check — the defect ledger item 30 records for the 0.3.0
# corpus, and ledger item 24 records for an untracked generator.
!analysis/measure_base_rate.py
!analysis/build_realpage_corpus.py
# The scheduled delta pass, added 2026-07-29. Tracked because it is the
# command OPEN-ITEMS.md tells a later session to run, and a scheduled
# measurement whose runner lives on one machine is not scheduled at all.
!analysis/run_delta_pass.py
# The baseline generator, tracked 2026-07-29. It produced DELTA-BASELINE.json,
# which is committed evidence the scheduled delta pass reads. An untracked
# generator of a committed artefact is the shape of items 24 and 34.
!analysis/make_baseline.py
# The capture verifier, tracked 2026-07-30. It is the thing that FAILS when the
# irreplaceable 2026-07-29 capture is missing or has rotted, and both
# run_delta_pass.py and make_baseline.py import it before loading those bytes. An
# untracked verifier is no verifier: it would exist on one machine, which is the
# same single-point-of-failure shape as the capture it protects (ledger item 55).
!analysis/verify_capture.py
# DELTA-REHEARSAL.json is deliberately NOT re-included. It is a zero-change
# delta produced by feeding one snapshot in as both sides, so it is not a
# measurement. Committing it would put a figure in the repository that a
# reader could mistake for one. It stays local, and `analysis/*` above
# already excludes it — recorded here so the exclusion is a decision.
DOSSIER_*.md
SECURITY_APPENDIX_*.md
DECISION.md
AUDIT-REPORT.md
.handover.md
.moat-handover.md

# Generated in CI by the security job: the resolved dependency set that
# pip-audit --strict audits. Regenerated every run; committing it would be a
# second copy of the resolution, free to drift from the real one.
requirements-audit.txt

# Generated overview docs with local filesystem paths
docs/skillwatch-overview.js
